e/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320792/field-3/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-320792/field-3/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320792" :question/id #uuid "7b8a9973-aa98-512e-bbfe-9875029cb267" :question/math-academy-id "q-320792" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ 4x+y=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | $1$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $2$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $5$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-2$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $1$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $2$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-2$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 1-4\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-320792/field-1" "q-320792/field-2" "q-320792/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320792"] :db/ensure [:kno