b013194ce1893aa56a78a6f8bf7f53980229b2cd0a90b1ec8d9ea8682f02" "q-102807/selection/42aad8c9648ae6eeb4e931398f4d9b83b0fca9cf72dbedf88e7e98319217f644" "q-102807/selection/3a7c7b5f081b8c6915021cf85a9fb7b21ea8e4814acab086f326a123f8652c4a" "q-102807/selection/a2b843f3302e216725307bdee2117325dcaf5c2638dc91f3e062585a6e31f490" "q-102807/selection/1bd8afa952ec5f012fd2822a6ffe13bc299cdd5d75d125183d6ba74bc69cf9df"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102807" :question/id #uuid "f0b10b3a-1c60-596e-980b-5212c6a85533" :question/math-academy-id "q-102807" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2y=x+3 \\\\ 7-y=-x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-x+2y=3 \\\\ x-y=-7.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-1)\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-102807/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102807"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275763/field-1/e3b46c3e63ee8ef5a071cd8ef5f7250114c0c6983477af061861d82a06039d46" :answer/id #uuid "c400020f-e6da-55bc-967a-f8d955e6aede" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275763/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ec87351c-1da9-51e1-8034-8ce932a81d90" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275763/field-1/e3b46c3e63ee8ef5a071cd8ef5f7250114c0c6983477af061861d82a06039d46" :answer-field/choices ["q-275763/field-1/e3b46c3e63ee8ef5a071cd8ef5f7250114c0c6983477af061861d82a06039d46"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275763/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "dbb32358-bc57-5a2a-8f4b-64778c96fef4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275763/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b8f60af5-c4a5-5f21-9325-062b02927d5e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275763/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-275763/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275763/field-3/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "6b765a90-99ed-59c1-b4df-dbd5b8aa7a77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275763/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "497a0375-f3a5-5b20-ad7d-5f9faaf74894" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275763/field-3/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-275763/field-3/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275763" :question/id #uuid "2837283f-7c61-55d2-a393-6b0e82a34b4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-275763" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3y=1-3x \\\\ x-2=-4y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-3$ |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $1$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $2$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+3y=1 \\\\ x+4y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-275763/field-1" "q-275763/field-2" "q-275763/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275763"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4508"] :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/assets/843dcd4359e4b61eb9715966fbbe6c26363ab5cfc57c55f94b6a41a73ec7feb1.png)\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/assets/b9ba240f93ee3ec8c02e9718d62342dca0e0855e24c7b34ed97758a6eb7c46b8.png) This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solution is $x=0$ and $y=2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4509"] :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $A\\mathbf{x} =\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/assets/240a1d2f7f93ec808127c9fa1791a77a43fcd7c0c84505540acc81c8b9fbc6e1.png)\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052845/assets/7850cbafc78f2cf2ce14ae7111064bf2f5a029f4d1b97b6d5ebfc09e7126f44e.png) This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=-3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
